            {
              "id": "8167a0e6-4644-430e-ade5-5f6e543fa889",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Playing It Up: With Loose Parts, Playpods, &amp;Adventure Playgrounds</strong></em> was written by Joan Almon, self-published through CreateSpace, February 2, 2017."
            },
            {
              "id": "ab5d1388-8ec3-44e6-bd15-c94bd18e5827",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "0aaa47c1-8a95-4fde-979d-e7dc7bd5d709",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Child-initiated, creative play is returning after decades of erosion. Through the hard work and dedicated efforts of play activists, new opportunities for play are arising, including the use of open-ended play materials in schools, parks, nature centers, and adventure playgrounds. Over 20 play initiatives are described in this book, with dozens of photographs that illustrate the power of play.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "1145dfb8-1c77-42cd-8967-2c0ad3805390",
              "type": "paragraph",
